# The shell and the counter, the counter below it (roadmap l4.md L2): the
# shell answers as ever, and the counter runs whenever the shell waits. The
# shell is the shell in C, a process, among init's (os-server.md P12; each
# with a thread of the OS server's), and the counter the module the root
# builds (TEST_COUNTER). DOSBox-X's shell starts in /: it cannot read the
# drives (docs/emulators.md).
program: shell
define: TEST_COUNTER
define: TEST_THREAD_REPORT
keys: echo hello\n
---
rx286, test build
@bochs /a$ echo hello
@mame /a$ echo hello
@dosbox-x /$ echo hello
hello
@bochs /a$
@mame /a$
@dosbox-x /$
rx286: thread root ran
rx286: thread printer ran
rx286: thread mouse ran
rx286: thread console ran
